	<!-- Portrait only, on every device family, matching the Android manifest's
	     android:screenOrientation="portrait". Every board in the collection is
	     laid out for a portrait screen. UIRequiresFullScreen is what lets the
	     build declare a restricted orientation set at all.

	     The wide-screen CSS of issue #93 is still here and still shipping — it
	     is what the browser version and a large phone use. What is NOT shipping
	     is the iPad *binary*: TARGETED_DEVICE_FAMILY went back to 1 because
	     iPad support has never been verified on real hardware (rotation, Split
	     View, Stage Manager) and the 13" screenshots App Store Connect demands
	     of a Universal app do not exist yet. Turning this back on is one line
	     here and one in project.pbxproj, once those two are done. -->
	<key>UIRequiresFullScreen</key>
	<true/>
